ids":["cite.long.record-257bm-i-cross2"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-i-cross2"],"id":"long.record-257bm-i-cross2","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.114 (Existence of a first crossing)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.114, p. 76, label record:257bm-i-cross2","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $E\\subseteq\\{2,3,\\ldots\\}$ be finite and suppose $X_E(2)>1/2$. There is a least $c\\in E$ such that\n$$\nX_{E\\cap[2,c)}(2)<\\frac12\n       <X_{E\\cap[2,c]}(2),\\qquad c\\ge4.\n$$\nPositivity of the summands makes the partial sums increasing. Their odd reduced denominators exclude equality with $1/2$, so the first crossing is strict on both sides. Finally $w_2+w_3=10/21<1/2$, which excludes a crossing before rank $4$. This is the finite crossing data used in the later exact-row constructions; the lower bound on $c$ and strictness are specific to these weights.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-i-cross2","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-i-cross2","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i-cross2%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.exists_first_localMersenne_crossing%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i-cross2%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.exists_first_localMersenne_crossing%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.exists_first_localMersenne_crossing"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-i-cross2","id":"field:22eca